# Closeness-check review queue (PLAN.md #45 Phase 5) — QUOTE_CANDIDATE/
# HOLD_TOO_LITTLE statements withheld from the DB, local-only. Contains raw
# extracted-statement text derived from copyrighted source material; a
# worse fit for permanent git history than for the database it came from.
closeness_review/

# Reference-grounding review queue (PLAN.md #45, 2026-07-28) — every
# UNGROUNDED/UNCERTAIN scripture reference stripped from a proposition's
# content by extract_propositions(), local-only. Same rationale as
# closeness_review/ above — a worse fit for permanent git history than for
# the database it came from.
reference_grounding_review/

# Reference-fabrication corpus-detection review queue (PLAN.md #45,
# 2026-07-28, Part 2 — scripts/detect_reference_fabrication.py). Every
# UNGROUNDED/UNCERTAIN scripture reference found by a corpus-wide,
# read-only detection pass over `propositions.content` against full
# reconstructed source text, local-only. Same rationale as
# closeness_review/ and reference_grounding_review/ above.
reference_fabrication_review/

# Layer 3 LLM reading-pass live-run review (PLAN.md #45.6, 2026-07-29) —
# per-item model verdicts + reasons from the first-ever live run of
# citation_verifier_layers.py's Layer 3, including full proposition text.
# Same rationale as the review queues above — local-only, not for git history.
layer3_llm_reading_pass_review/

# Generator bypass-proofing live-proof review (PLAN.md #45.8, 2026-07-30) —
# Phase 5's live-run output: real extraction/arbitration results and
# would-have-been storage payloads for the three-document proof, storage
# itself always intercepted, never written. Same rationale as the review
# queues above — local-only, not for git history.
generator_live_proof_review/

# PLAN.md #46 human-calibration judging set (2026-07-30) — contains
# reconstructed full source passages from copyrighted third-party
# transcripts, for Alex's own reading/judging pass. Same rationale as the
# review queues above — a worse fit for permanent git history than for the
# database it came from.
calibration_review/

# Full propositions backfill run log (PLAN.md #17/#49, 2026-07-30) —
# incremental per-document JSONL checkpoint for the v3.1-prompt full
# backfill run (scripts/run_full_backfill.py). Contains generated
# proposition content for crash-recovery/resumability purposes only; the
# database itself is the durable record. Same rationale as the review
# queues above — local-only, not for git history.
backfill_run_review/

# PLAN.md #46 position-layer calibration batch (2026-07-30) — draft position
# text generated via the real gather_evidence()/generate_position_text()
# path, for Alex's blind-judging pass. Nothing here is stored to the
# positions/position_evidence tables. Same rationale as the review queues
# above — local-only, not for git history.
position_calibration_review/

# Book-chapter live-proof review (2026-07-31) — real Run A/Run B proposition
# output, reconciliation dicts, grounding/arbitration evidence, and
# redundancy-check results for the Andrew Murray "The True Vine" chapter-
# scoped extraction proof (scripts/propositions.py's split_book_into_
# chapters()/_extract_and_store_book_chapters()/process_book_document()).
# Storage was always intercepted this session, never written. Same
# rationale as the review queues above — local-only, not for git history.
book_chapter_live_proof_review/

# Phase 2 teacher-name guard live-run artifact (local, regenerated on demand)
scripts/teacher_name_guard_live_results.json
# Phase 2 residual prose-scan live-run artifact (local, regenerated on demand)
